    "unresolved": [],
    "note": "Positions are LOCAL to this deck and are not atlas positions — the deck is re-laid-out from its own cards, which is the whole point. Anything that draws this must say so.",
    "named_by": "deck-cartographer",
    "cartographer_notes": [
      "Read against the 2026-09-11 map (decklist_sha256 b394917f, 89 cards, 7 cities). The previous deck-cartographer.json (2026-08-13, V3 layout, sha 0480aaf7) had been merged onto today's ids before this run and put THE PIVOT TURN on the tutor cluster, BUYING TURNS on the protection instants, THE SEARCH PARTY on the rocks and THE SIDE DOOR on the cost reducers. Where a cluster is genuinely the same as V3's (city-0, city-1 and its three hoods, MAKING ROOM, BUYING TURNS, THE SEARCH PARTY, THE SIDE DOOR) the old name is kept so engine.json's evidence notes, which cite labels by name, stay readable; engine.json's city ids are still V3's and need a re-run.",
      "city-6 is three Dinosaur cost reducers and Blasphemous Act, which the space filed here on its own 'costs {1} less' clause. Functionally the Act is the one-sided wipe paired with Temple Altisaur (city-0-hood-1), which engine.json reads as the deck's board-clear; the name THE DISCOUNTS covers its cost clause honestly, but do not describe city-6 as the wipe. It is the deck's odd placement, not a card that does not belong.",
      "city-0-hood-0 is eleven Dinosaurs including the commander, and every one triggers on entry or on attack; four of them (Gishath, Etali, Ghalta and Mavren, Quartzwood Crasher) trigger on the swing rather than on arrival, which is why V3's PAYS ON ARRIVAL was retired for this hood.",
      "city-0-hood-3 is four draw engines. Runic Armasaur is the odd member: it draws off an opponent's activations, not off big bodies or Dinosaur combat damage like the other three. It belongs to the job (refill), not to the trigger.",
      "The enrage remnant is split across borders: Trapjaw Tyrant is in MAKING ROOM on its exile text, Wrathful Raptors and Temple Altisaur are in SCALES WITH THE BOARD. Prose about the remnant must name it across two cities.",
      "city-1-hood-1: Kessig Wolf Run and Rogue's Passage are the two non-fixing members, which is why the hood is named for both jobs. Secluded Courtyard and Unclaimed Territory in the same hood make creature-restricted mana; per deck-facts, Unclaimed Territory cannot pay Belbe's Portal, Monster Manual, Rogue's Passage or Kessig Wolf Run, and Secluded Courtyard pays only Dinosaur abilities.",
      "city-4 holds four protection instants and Carnage Tyrant, a hexproof uncounterable body that insures itself; the split reads clean.",
      "city-2, city-3, city-4, city-5 and city-6 each have a single neighbourhood with exactly their parent's membership. Those hoods are left unnamed on purpose: a hood that repeats its city is not narrower than it, and the deterministic fallback is the honest label."
    ]
  },
